      "title": "William Tell Cast Iron Mechanical Bank Book of Knowledge Reproduction",
      "description": "<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;color:#222;max-width:760px;\"><h2 style=\"font-size:22px;margin:0 0 12px;\">William Tell Cast Iron Mechanical Bank</h2><p>William Tell, a tiny red apple, and a castle make this cast-iron coin bank a whole scene in ten inches. This vintage Book of Knowledge reproduction has a painted green base, a castle tower, and both figures, with the red apple still present. The underside carries the cast-in Book of Knowledge reproduction mark.</p><h3 style=\"font-size:18px;margin:20px 0 8px;\">Condition</h3><p>Paint loss, surface wear, and rust spotting, especially on the base. The coin mechanism has not been fully tested.</p><h3 style=\"font-size:18px;margin:20px 0 8px;\">Details</h3><p>Painted cast iron. The bank measures 10 \u00d7 3\u00bc \u00d7 6\u00bc inches and weighs 4 lb 5.2 oz.</p><h3 style=\"font-size:18px;margin:20px 0 8px;\">Included</h3><p>One William Tell mechanical coin bank, as pictured.</p><h3 style=\"font-size:18px;margin:20px 0 8px;\">Packing &amp; Shipping</h3><p>The cast-iron base will be braced in a sturdy corrugated box with clearance around the figures and projecting parts. Buyer-paid calculated shipping. Returns accepted within 30 days with buyer-paid return shipping.</p></div>",
